            <p>Travel by train focuses on comfort, predictability, and pleasure. The passengers do not experience fatigue and congestion in the roadways and enjoy regular schedules and ample seats. Away from city rush, train journeys let calm settle in naturally. This progressive change turns the journey into an evocative and memorable experience. Some choose silence instead, just watching wide canyons unfold beyond the glass. Moments stretch without hurry here. </p>

            <h2>Rail Routes Serving this Region </h2>
            <p>The Grand Canyon is served by rail routes that link to nearby gateway cities and regional locations. These are the routes leading to northern Arizona, and the transfers are arranged in such a way that the travelers to the park area find it easy to reach there. The train system can be a viable alternative because there are well-developed rail lines. </p>

